= The End of Anderson

Former Premier James Anderson, previously renowned for leading the Conservative Party to its first electoral success in Grit-Dominated Saskatchewan, has resigned his leadership of the party over the catastrophic results of the election. A section of the CPS right-wing, calling themselves 'True Blue Tories' have been pressing Anderson on his cooperation with the left-leaning Progressive Party and his lack of support for the CPC in seats not contested provincially by the CPS. Some support, however, still remains for a broad anti-liberal alliance. Thus, the party's acting president, John Diefenbaker, has called a leadership convention to replace Anderson. 

11 nominations have been drawn so far though it remains to be seen how many Tories actually choose to accept them. [? if cps_polls < 20 : To many, it seems the CPS is electorally moribund, destined to become an insignificant force between the LPS and [+ party_names.ccf +]. ?]

