= Diefenbaker

John Diefenbaker is a wildcard. With a background as a defence lawyer, he has been unsuccessful in attempts to enter the Legislature despite close results in 1929. Still, he is the standing President of the CPS. 

He represents a strand of the party that supports most strongly a strong welfare system and increased government intervention; colloquially, the Red Tories or a form of Paternalistic Conservatism. He is expected to draft a Red Tory reform-programme for the CPS as a middle-ground between the LPS and [+ party_names.ccf +] platforms. Whether it will succeed in attracting the masses of disaffected people remains to be seen. 

The devasting loss means that he will likely collaborate with us to ensure his party's survival, whether he wants to or not. We can expect him to participate in saw-offs with us and support most reform-minded legislation introduced. 

