= MacPherson

Murdoch Macpherson, also known by M.A. MacPherson, represents a continuation of traditional Saskatchewan Toryism. He was Anderson's Attorney General, during which time he negotiated the return of natural resource rights to Saskatchewan, withheld by Ottawa during the province's formation. He also served as the unofficial liaison between the Relief Commission and the Cooperative Coalition and later took on the Treasurer position. It is expected that he will focus on questions of administration and public finance as leader and attempt to leverage fears of the LPS machine once again running rampant in the Civil Service. In addition, he has his own social-reform credentials, being in favour of unemployment insurance, pro-labour reform, and electoral reform. 

There are not high hopes that he will be able to reverse the party's sinking fortunes. However, he may be able to leverage his connections in the Federal Party to pull in organizational and financial support from out East. 

While the party has been badly damaged by the recent election, MacPherson is strident in not forming official ties with the [+ party_names.ccf +]. Thus, we can cross off any formal working partnership with MacPherson's CPS though electoral cooperation may be on the table to prevent an outright Liberal majority. 

