= Bryant

James Fraser Bryant is a former Cabinet member of the Anderson government whose leadership signals a continuation of Anderson's social policies. He is primarily known for rewriting the School Act to prohibit religious symbols in schools and strengthen the usage of English as the language of instruction. Like the other Tories, he is in favour of de-politicizing the civil service, primarily as a measure to prevent another LPS machine from running day-to-day operations. He is among many Saskatchewanians who engaged with the KKK.

His strong British-nativist stance earns him a swathe of attacks by the Liberal Party, likening him to the worst of the KKK. His election consolidates the traditionalist factions of the CPS, committed to making social issues a prominent feature in the campaign alongside anti-corruption policies. Bryant will likely use us as a punching bag, out of opposition to our Socialist and Socialistic tendencies. 